# D-094 chatbox re-skin: @mentions. Script 84 builds the chatbox lines (RuneLite calls it ChatBuilder). After each
# message is read from the chat history, a message that contains the viewer's own name (tags removed, any case) and
# was not sent by the viewer is wrapped in the mention colour. Game messages (type 0) are left alone.
# Locals (RuneLite's ChatBuilder overlay comments): o0 own name, i11 type, o19 sender, o21 text, o24 timestamp.
# Second hunk (D-096): public chat lines (types 1 and 2, LABEL452) look the sender up in the roster the server writes to
# tp_chat_roster (162:579) as ";name=<prefix>;" (lowercase, tags removed); a listed sender is drawn as prefix + name +
# "</col>", the prefix being the rank or donator icon and name colour. The client's own crown tag is removed with the other
# tags. Only the drawn line changes: o19 itself (used later for the name's menu ops) is untouched; new locals i25, o26.
